Real end-to-end CLI transcript of `bin/fm-send.sh` steering a real tmux pane, captured by
temporarily instrumenting a scratch (non-committed) copy of tests/fm-send-shell-pane-refusal.test.sh
to print the literal captured stdout/stderr (SEND_OUT) that a captain running `fm-send` would see,
in place of the test's normal string-match assertions. The tracked test file itself is unmodified;
this transcript exists only to show the actual product-facing text behind those assertions.

This exercises upstream #3823 ("stop ringing steering doorbells into dead panes"), merged in this
batch, and the fork's follow-up fixture fix (commit 2b7875e) that re-aligned three assertions to the
merged contract. Command: `bash tests/fm-send-shell-pane-refusal.test.sh` (run in place, unmodified,
separately, to confirm pass/fail); transcript below from the instrumented scratch copy.

[fm-send CLI transcript] exit=0
fm-send: doorbell not typed because the agent in %0 has exited; the steer is durably recorded at .../home/state/deadmate.inbox/001.msg for recovery (stuck-crewmate-recovery), and the watcher will not re-ring a dead pane
---
ok - an ordinary steer to a shell-held endpoint is recorded, never typed, and reported as reaching an exited agent

[fm-send CLI transcript] exit=1
error: nothing was sent to %0: its terminal is held by a shell, not a live agent, so the worker's agent has exited (verdict=no-agent; ...). The text was NOT typed. Recover the worker before resending.
---
ok - a harness-native steer to that same pane is refused outright and never typed

[fm-send CLI transcript] exit=0
---
ok - the same pane shape with a live agent in the foreground is rung, not refused

[fm-send CLI transcript] exit=1
error: text was typed into %2 but its agent exited to a shell before the submission could be confirmed (verdict=agent-lost; ...); no agent received it. Verify the pane with fm-peek.sh and recover the worker before resending.
---
ok - an agent that exits to a shell mid-send is never reported as having received the steer

[fm-send CLI transcript] exit=0
fm-send: no live agent at %3 - the doorbell line was typed there but its agent exited to a shell before the submission could be confirmed, so no agent received it. The steer is durably recorded at .../ringlossmate.inbox/001.msg and waits for a live agent; the watcher re-rings and escalates it. Recover the worker rather than resending, or the record is duplicated.
---
ok - an agent that exits to a shell during the ring itself is never reported as having received the doorbell

[fm-send CLI transcript] exit=0
---
ok - a doorbell bound to one tmux server never reaches a same-id pane on another

[fm-send CLI transcript] exit=0
fm-send: doorbell not sent to %0 - its recorded endpoint could not be verified to exist on the expected tmux server, so nothing was typed there. The steer is durably recorded at .../unresolvablemate.inbox/001.msg and waits for a live agent; the watcher re-rings and escalates it. Recover or re-verify the worker's endpoint rather than resending, or the record is duplicated.
---
ok - a doorbell bound to a tmux server that no longer exists is refused, never rerouted to an ambient same-id pane

ok - cleanup runs its tmux calls exactly once and never risks the default socket, even with the wrong-server directory already gone
all fm-send shell-pane refusal tests passed

