Remote-path counterpart, same instrumentation technique applied to
tests/fm-send-remote-delivery.test.sh's `err` capture in
test_remote_ring_no_agent_names_absent_endpoint, exercising bin/fm-remote-secondmate-control.sh
cmd_send against a fake Herdr backend:

[fm-send-remote CLI transcript] exit=0
notice: doorbell not typed because the agent in fm-remote:p1 has exited; the steer is durably recorded at .../remote-no-agent-rhome/state/parent-route/rsm.inbox/001.msg for recovery
---
ok - fm-send remote: a doorbell to a no-agent Herdr endpoint reports absence and never fails the send
all fm-send-remote-delivery tests passed

Both transcripts match the merged upstream #3823 wording exactly ("agent ... has exited",
"doorbell not typed", "for recovery", "will not re-ring a dead pane") rather than the fork's
retired pre-merge wording ("no live agent", "waits for a live agent") that the prior review round's
declined test finding had flagged as failing. The fork's fixture fix (2b7875e) is confirmed correct
against real product output, not just against its own updated assertions.
